<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="065" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>F4 — a save with no TargetEntity bypasses EntityAccessFilter entirely, lands in the shared container, and is then profiled and RAG-indexed</title>
    <phase>5 Remediation — authorization</phase>
    <gate>blocked — requires 061</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Changes the contract of the project's primary save path. Tags include bff-api + auth + security. The Word ribbon quick-save currently depends on the bypassed branch.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Touches the save spine — the best-evidenced, most reproduce-first-tested part of the project. Breaking it regresses FR-06 through FR-12 at once.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits the save spine in `OfficeService.cs` + `OfficeEndpoints.cs` + the Word commands client. Highest-collision surface in the project.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>061</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, auth, authorization, security, office, frontend, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>6-10 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>`POST /office/save` treats association as optional, so a request with no `TargetEntity` passes `EntityAccessFilter` untouched and lands in the tenant-wide default container — and every Word ribbon quick-save takes exactly that path. Make the target required and give the ribbon a real container.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. The save spine is this project's strongest work — change it carefully and keep every existing save test green.</role>

  <goal>No save reaches storage without an authorized association, and the Word ribbon quick-save files to a container resolved the same way the pane does.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Found 2026-09-21 by the Fable review (`notes/fable-review-2026-09-21.md` §2 finding F4, §9).

      `OfficeEndpoints.cs:414-462` — "Association is optional". `EntityAccessFilter.cs:201-212` calls
      `next()` when the target is absent, so **no resource check runs at all**. `OfficeService.cs:186-195`
      then falls back to `EmailProcessing:DefaultContainerId` (provisioned from `SPE_DEFAULT_CONTAINER_ID`,
      `appsettings.template.json:233`). Upload is app-only (`:622-627`), the row create is app-only (`:702`),
      and `TriggerAiProcessing` / `RagIndex` both default true (`Models/Office/SaveRequest.cs:72,413`).

      Same effect for `account` and `contact` targets, which have no `sprk_document` lookup column
      (`OfficeEndpoints.cs:425-430`).

      **The premise in the code is false.** `OfficeService.cs:143-145` and `:341-343` assert the no-target
      branch *"exists for the contract rather than for traffic"*. Since task 037 that is wrong:
      `quickSaveHelpers.ts:172-200` (`buildDocumentSaveRequest`) sends no `targetEntity`, and
      `word/commands/index.ts:151-153` posts it. **Every Word ribbon quick-save takes the bypassed path** and
      lands in the shared, BU-agnostic container.

      Not a data-safety bug today — the container fails closed if unset — but the isolation argument written
      in the code no longer describes real traffic, and the authorization bypass is real.

      Task 076's owner sanction (acting-user BU) is the reference for how the ribbon should resolve a
      container.
    </background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="this task">Fix BOTH halves. Making `TargetEntity` required without giving the ribbon a container breaks Word quick-save; giving the ribbon a container without requiring the target leaves the bypass open.</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">Every existing save test must stay green. This spine carries FR-06 through FR-12 and five reproduce-first regression suites (039/045/046/047/054/055) — reconcile the count, do not merely assert "tests pass".</constraint>
    <constraint source="this task">If the account/contact no-lookup-column case cannot carry an association, define its behaviour explicitly rather than letting it fall into the default-container branch.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The association check stays in `EntityAccessFilter`; this task removes the bypass, it does not move the check into the handler.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Publish-size delta against a fresh master build; CVE check.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">REPRODUCE-FIRST: prove a save with no `TargetEntity` is accepted, reaches the default container, and is RAG-indexed — with no resource authorization anywhere in the path. Record verbatim.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`TargetEntity` is required on `/office/save`; a request without one is rejected with a problem response before any upload or row create.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Word ribbon quick-save sends a real target and resolves a container the way the pane does (acting-user BU). It still succeeds end to end.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The account/contact case has explicitly defined behaviour, stated in the task note and covered by a test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The false comments at `OfficeService.cs:143-145` and `:341-343` are corrected to describe what the code now does.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SEED BOTH DIRECTIONS on the new requirement: remove it, show the negative test RED; restore, show GREEN. Record both.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every pre-existing save test is green and the count is reconciled explicitly against 12,379 passed / 0 failed — a regression here is worse than the finding.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Task 061's guard no longer flags this route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">ArchTests green; publish size and CVE reported.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the required-target contract, the ribbon path, the account/contact case, the unchanged happy paths and the seed directions. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any shipped client legitimately needs to save without an association — check Outlook's paths and the e2e specs before concluding it does not — STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6. Requiring the target then becomes a breaking contract change needing an owner decision and a migration path.</trigger>
    <trigger>If resolving a container for the ribbon requires new Dataverse or SPE surface rather than reusing the pane's resolution, STOP — that is a design decision beyond this task's scope.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>/conflict-check (bff-api hot path — highest collision file in the project).</step>
    <step>Reproduce the bypass end to end; record verbatim.</step>
    <step>Enumerate every in-repo caller of `/office/save` and confirm which send no target. Do this before changing the contract.</step>
    <step>Give the ribbon a resolved container first, so the requirement does not break it.</step>
    <step>Make `TargetEntity` required; define the account/contact behaviour; correct the false comments.</step>
    <step>Tests; seed both directions; reconcile the full-suite count explicitly.</step>
    <step>Build, full suite, ArchTests, publish size, CVE.</step>
    <step>Write `notes/065-require-target-entity.md`. Update TASK-INDEX.md: 065 → ✅.</step>
  </steps>

